  best magnitude anywhere on the frontier: 0.232 dB
  best phase     anywhere on the frontier: 2.6 deg

  ⭐ READ THIS AS THE RESULT. Minimum phase is the MAXIMUM-LEAD realisation of
  a given magnitude (any other causal realisation is min-phase x an all-pass,
  and an all-pass only ADDS lag). So if the measured phase cannot be reached by
  a min-phase cascade that also matches the magnitude, NO causal linear element
  of ANY order can supply this target -- which is a stronger statement than
  session 50's reachability result (that ruled out the elements the model
  contains; this rules out the whole CLASS).

=== 2d. CAN THE PHASE MEASUREMENT'S KNOWN BIAS EXPLAIN THE SHORTFALL? ===
  The blend-axis quadratic gives Q = Re(g1) EXACTLY but r = sqrt(|g1|^2 + H)
  with H the band's harmonic power, so cos(theta) = Q/r is biased TOWARDS 90 deg
  and r is an UPPER BOUND on the fundamental. Correcting it moves theta away
  from 90 deg, which REDUCES the required lead over 127-640 Hz -- so it is a
  live explanation. Sizing it as the implied harmonic-to-fundamental power:
       f    th_ped th needed     d deg  implied H/P
      40     138.2     108.0     -30.1   impossible
      50     142.5      92.2     -50.3   impossible
      64     134.1      78.6     -55.4    sign flip
      80     115.9      69.9     -46.0    sign flip
     101      95.3      61.6     -33.7    sign flip
     127      75.0      50.7     -24.3          5.0
     160      56.5      36.6     -19.9          1.1
