     254      56.6      14.1     -42.4          2.1
     403      81.4      24.8     -56.7         36.1
     508      74.2      33.5     -40.6          8.3
     640      87.3      38.6     -48.6        265.1
     806     100.8      53.4     -47.4    sign flip
    1016      96.6      56.0     -40.6    sign flip
    1613      59.2      44.0     -15.2          1.0

  'implied H/P' is the harmonic-to-fundamental POWER ratio the bias would need
  in order to reconcile the measurement with the min-phase fit. H/P = 0.1 is
  ~32%% THD; H/P = 1 is more harmonic power than fundamental. 'impossible' means
  the bias would have to act in the WRONG DIRECTION (deflate r), which harmonic
  power cannot do; 'sign flip' means no inflation of any size suffices.

  DELAY CHECK: best-fit pure delay -0.113 ms leaves 32.3 deg rms; a FLAT offset
  of -38.1 deg leaves 12.9 deg rms. Shortfall span -56.7 to -15.2 deg over a 40x
  frequency range => FLAT, not proportional to f: a delay-compensation mismatch on the OD path is
     EXCLUDED as the cause.
  => the bias CANNOT explain the shortfall at the bands that carry it.

